  {
   "n": 3,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>\n\tFor an ideal op-amp, which of the following properties is not correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Open loop voltage gain is infinite"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Input resistance is infinite"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Slew rate is infinite"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "CMRR is zero"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(d)<br />\n\tFor ideal op-amp, CMRR is infinite. i.e. differential gain is infinite and common-mode gain is zero</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>\n\tFor the circuit given below,</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/1784116f90cc593bdffd.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tIf <em>X</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>X</em><sub>2</sub> are inductors and <em>X</em><sub>3</sub> is capacitor, then the circuit is know as</p>",
   "options": [
